Cowan's definition is the only one I've ever seen...

It is the correct one, and the one we've been using.



In general, you can deduce:
	broda ko'a |- broda zi'o (but not the other way around!)
for all broda, and anything for ko'a (including noda).

Not including noda! noda is not a possible value for ko'a,
indeed noda is not a value, it is a quantified variable.

{noda catra la djim} = "There is no x such that x killed Jim."
does not entail {zi'o catra la djim}.

